1
00:01:37,950 --> 00:01:43,920
[Small Town Remedy]

2
00:01:44,289 --> 00:01:46,850
[Episode 5]

3
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,870
I said I really didn't see her.

4
00:01:48,870 --> 00:01:50,930
She just came rushing out of nowhere.

5
00:01:51,120 --> 00:01:53,280
And my vehicle's pretty big,

6
00:01:53,590 --> 00:01:54,990
so there are blind spots.

7
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:56,789
Um,

8
00:01:57,710 --> 00:01:58,350
the emergency room.

9
00:01:58,350 --> 00:01:59,509
That way, that way.

10
00:01:59,509 --> 00:01:59,920
Okay, okay.

11
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:02,520
She fell off her electric scooter
right there.

12
00:02:03,000 --> 00:02:03,790
Honey,

13
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:05,810
what happened?

14
00:02:07,430 --> 00:02:08,190
Why are you crying?

15
00:02:08,190 --> 00:02:09,080
Where's our daughter?

16
00:02:09,080 --> 00:02:10,280
What happened to her?

17
00:02:11,590 --> 00:02:12,400
Where is she?

18
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:13,590
Where is she?

19
00:02:15,910 --> 00:02:17,000
Family of Zhang Jiao,

20
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:18,130
please come with me.

21
00:02:27,190 --> 00:02:28,390
What happened to her?

22
00:02:31,470 --> 00:02:33,520
The patient has suffered
severe traumatic brain injury

23
00:02:33,520 --> 00:02:35,450
and developed a brain herniation.

24
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:38,000
Her condition is critical.

25
00:02:38,960 --> 00:02:40,030
Without surgery,

26
00:02:41,750 --> 00:02:43,410
she may not survive the night.

27
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:46,430
It's all my fault.

28
00:02:46,430 --> 00:02:47,750
The... the s-surgery.

29
00:02:47,800 --> 00:02:51,000
Yes, we'll go ahead
with the surgery, Doctor. We'll do it.

30
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:52,750
None of our doctors here

31
00:02:52,750 --> 00:02:54,240
can perform this surgery.

32
00:02:55,360 --> 00:02:56,760
We can only do the surgery

33
00:02:57,240 --> 00:02:58,120
if a highly skilled specialist

34
00:02:58,120 --> 00:02:59,450
is willing to come here.

35
00:02:59,750 --> 00:03:00,560
Doctor!

36
00:03:00,630 --> 00:03:01,430
Please get up.

37
00:03:01,520 --> 00:03:02,560
You can't do this.

38
00:03:02,960 --> 00:03:04,400
I... could I

39
00:03:04,840 --> 00:03:06,150
ask you to help us

40
00:03:07,000 --> 00:03:08,000
find someone?

41
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:10,590
We could take her to a bigger hospital,

42
00:03:10,590 --> 00:03:12,400
or bring a specialist here.

43
00:03:13,080 --> 00:03:14,960
-Please do the surgery my daughter needs.
-I'm begging you.

44
00:03:14,960 --> 00:03:16,360
Please save my daughter.

45
00:03:16,800 --> 00:03:18,079
I'm begging you.

46
00:03:19,190 --> 00:03:20,590
She's still so young.

47
00:03:20,590 --> 00:03:21,960
Please...

48
00:03:21,960 --> 00:03:23,150
She's so young.

49
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:16,070
I'll do it.

50
00:04:27,600 --> 00:04:28,390
I'll do it.

51
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:37,570
Thank you... Thank you!

52
00:04:37,800 --> 00:04:38,600
Thank you!

53
00:04:40,950 --> 00:04:41,600
Thank you!

54
00:04:42,310 --> 00:04:43,040
Thank you...

55
00:04:45,240 --> 00:04:46,120
She's lost too much blood.

56
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:46,920
We need an emergency blood transfusion.

57
00:04:46,920 --> 00:04:47,830
Start rapid fluid resuscitation.

58
00:04:47,830 --> 00:04:49,560
I'll check with the blood bank.

59
00:04:56,560 --> 00:04:56,870
[Hand Sanitising Station]

60
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:57,680
[Hand Sanitising Station]

61
00:04:57,850 --> 00:05:00,890
[Hand Sanitising Station]
[Touch-free Faucet]

62
00:05:05,160 --> 00:05:06,000
Blood pressure?

63
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:07,060
Ninety over sixty.

64
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:08,830
Mannitol, 100 mL.

65
00:05:08,830 --> 00:05:09,760
Run it wide open.

66
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:19,430
Mannitol, 100 mL. Wide open.

67
00:05:20,040 --> 00:05:22,700
Prepare povidone-iodine,
hydrogen peroxide,

68
00:05:22,870 --> 00:05:23,930
and normal saline.

69
00:05:28,630 --> 00:05:29,760
Forceps. Scissors.

70
00:05:42,360 --> 00:05:44,490
The patient's scalp is badly damaged,

71
00:05:45,120 --> 00:05:45,920
and rock fragments

72
00:05:45,920 --> 00:05:48,250
and other debris are visible in the wound.

73
00:05:50,390 --> 00:05:51,390
Get me soapy water

74
00:05:52,040 --> 00:05:53,270
and sterile gauze.

75
00:06:04,510 --> 00:06:05,310
Saline.

76
00:06:09,040 --> 00:06:10,120
I said saline!

77
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:11,160
Sorry, Dr. Liu.

78
00:06:11,430 --> 00:06:12,390
Focus.

79
00:06:32,310 --> 00:06:34,110
Povidone-iodine. Get it ready.

80
00:06:39,510 --> 00:06:41,240
Prepare to irrigate the wound.

81
00:06:41,310 --> 00:06:41,840
Forceps.

82
00:06:50,870 --> 00:06:52,200
Debridement complete.

83
00:06:52,310 --> 00:06:54,270
Disinfect again
and drape the surgical site.

84
00:06:54,270 --> 00:06:55,100
Prepare for surgery.

85
00:06:55,100 --> 00:07:00,830
[Fucheng Funeral Services]

86
00:07:03,150 --> 00:07:08,960
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

87
00:07:09,050 --> 00:07:09,890
[Fucheng Funeral Services]

88
00:07:22,120 --> 00:07:23,380
[Fucheng Funeral Services]

89
00:07:24,660 --> 00:07:28,170
[Bicycle Parking]

90
00:07:34,680 --> 00:07:35,940
What are you two doing?

91
00:07:41,830 --> 00:07:43,190
Which funeral home are you from?

92
00:07:43,190 --> 00:07:44,270
Business around Xiaoximen

93
00:07:44,270 --> 00:07:44,680
has always belonged

94
00:07:44,680 --> 00:07:46,040
to 1314 Funeral Services.

95
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:47,720
You'd better learn the rules.

96
00:07:49,720 --> 00:07:51,580
And why are you getting physical?

97
00:07:58,480 --> 00:07:59,159
[Notice: CCTV in Operation]

98
00:07:59,180 --> 00:08:00,010
[Please Behave Appropriately]

99
00:08:00,050 --> 00:08:02,580
[Operating Room]
[Authorized Personnel Only]

100
00:08:02,690 --> 00:08:03,520
[Authorized Personnel Only]
[Keep Quiet]

101
00:08:08,880 --> 00:08:13,930
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

102
00:08:16,120 --> 00:08:16,920
Sis,

103
00:08:17,360 --> 00:08:18,560
see those two?

104
00:08:18,720 --> 00:08:20,950
They came straight here
to steal our business.

105
00:08:20,950 --> 00:08:22,410
So, did you two get into it?

106
00:08:22,830 --> 00:08:24,230
I put them in their place.

107
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:25,270
You did?

108
00:08:25,950 --> 00:08:27,150
Got it under control.

109
00:08:30,360 --> 00:08:31,760
Breaking the rules, huh?

110
00:08:33,789 --> 00:08:35,549
He looks a lot like that guy

111
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,200
from that new-style funeral business.

112
00:08:38,870 --> 00:08:40,000
It must be those two.

113
00:08:41,480 --> 00:08:42,150
Got it.

114
00:08:52,150 --> 00:08:52,750
Hello,

115
00:08:53,440 --> 00:08:55,000
I'm the owner of 1314 Funeral Services,

116
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,720
and my name is Ai Chen.

117
00:08:58,320 --> 00:08:59,360
Xu Jie.

118
00:09:12,480 --> 00:09:14,940
Mr. Xu, you're quite impatient,
aren't you?

119
00:09:15,960 --> 00:09:17,720
The surgery isn't even over,

120
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:21,060
and you're already here
trying to snatch the business.

121
00:09:21,200 --> 00:09:22,550
To be honest,

122
00:09:23,630 --> 00:09:25,840
I haven't been in Fucheng long,

123
00:09:26,320 --> 00:09:28,630
but I've already built up
a few good connections

124
00:09:28,630 --> 00:09:30,090
for getting information.

125
00:09:31,200 --> 00:09:32,800
Oh, you've got connections.

126
00:09:34,510 --> 00:09:35,550
Xiaoximen Hospital

127
00:09:35,550 --> 00:09:37,080
is my territory.

128
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:39,300
But since you're new here,

129
00:09:39,480 --> 00:09:40,670
let's consider this a chance
to become friends.

130
00:09:40,670 --> 00:09:41,750
This job's yours.

131
00:09:42,480 --> 00:09:43,550
Go talk to them.

132
00:09:48,000 --> 00:09:50,000
Ms. Ai, you're pretty slick.

133
00:09:51,440 --> 00:09:52,440
Setting me up, huh?

134
00:09:52,440 --> 00:09:53,770
Come on, don't say that.

135
00:09:53,870 --> 00:09:54,600
Their kid

136
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:55,550
is still fighting for her life in there.

137
00:09:55,550 --> 00:09:57,910
If I go talk to her parents
about funeral arrangements now,

138
00:09:57,910 --> 00:09:59,360
they'd beat me to death!

139
00:10:02,630 --> 00:10:04,200
Let's stay calm

140
00:10:03,240 --> 00:10:06,550
[No smoking] [Keep quiet]

141
00:10:04,630 --> 00:10:06,200
and wait for the results together.

142
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:06,840
No, no.

143
00:10:07,670 --> 00:10:08,930
I said the job's yours.

144
00:10:10,120 --> 00:10:11,180
You guys wait here.

145
00:10:20,960 --> 00:10:21,390
Chen,

146
00:10:22,270 --> 00:10:22,960
how'd it go?

147
00:10:22,960 --> 00:10:25,160
They won't budge, no matter what we say.

148
00:10:25,200 --> 00:10:26,860
We need to teach them a lesson.

149
00:10:28,200 --> 00:10:29,360
Time to take matters into our own hands.

150
00:10:29,360 --> 00:10:30,150
What do you have in mind?

151
00:10:30,150 --> 00:10:32,880
Do you think I'd come up
with something that fast?

152
00:10:34,510 --> 00:10:36,370
Keep an eye on things here in a bit.

153
00:10:36,600 --> 00:10:38,030
Don't stare now—

154
00:10:38,030 --> 00:10:40,030
just keep an eye on them discreetly.

155
00:10:40,480 --> 00:10:42,240
I'm going to the inpatient department

156
00:10:42,240 --> 00:10:43,390
to talk things over with those two

157
00:10:43,390 --> 00:10:45,120
who actually have some brains.

158
00:10:55,750 --> 00:10:59,200
[Operating Room Integrated Control System]

159
00:10:57,150 --> 00:10:59,680
Anesthesia, we're beginning the procedure.

160
00:11:13,550 --> 00:11:14,280
Scalp clips.

161
00:11:37,480 --> 00:11:38,840
The skull is shattered.

162
00:11:38,870 --> 00:11:41,270
We need to remove
the loose bone fragments.

163
00:12:08,030 --> 00:12:10,290
Dr. Liu, let me wipe the blood
off for you.

164
00:12:10,630 --> 00:12:12,290
Clear the epidural hematoma.

165
00:12:38,440 --> 00:12:39,510
I can see it.

166
00:12:39,750 --> 00:12:40,390
Anesthesiologist,

167
00:12:40,390 --> 00:12:42,050
how are the patient's vitals?

168
00:12:42,600 --> 00:12:44,000
Blood pressure, 93 over 62.

169
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:44,750
Heart rate, 111.

170
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:46,350
Microscope. Change gloves.

171
00:12:51,790 --> 00:12:53,120
Your left hand, Dr. Liu.

172
00:12:56,070 --> 00:13:00,590
[Operating Room Integrated Control System]

173
00:12:59,960 --> 00:13:01,600
He's getting way too cocky.

174
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:03,800
Don't we need to do something about him?

175
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,960
If everyone did what he does—

176
00:13:06,200 --> 00:13:07,600
camping outside the operating room

177
00:13:07,600 --> 00:13:08,510
and swooping in to snatch the business

178
00:13:08,510 --> 00:13:09,870
whenever someone died—

179
00:13:09,870 --> 00:13:11,240
wouldn't everything descend into chaos?

180
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:12,840
T-The families would hate us for it.

181
00:13:12,840 --> 00:13:13,570
I'm serious.

182
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:15,030
I'm willing to lose money over this,

183
00:13:15,030 --> 00:13:15,960
you understand?

184
00:13:16,030 --> 00:13:17,760
But I can't let him win this one.

185
00:13:18,670 --> 00:13:20,390
Get your dad to bring some people over.

186
00:13:20,390 --> 00:13:21,870
We'll take them down.

187
00:13:22,550 --> 00:13:23,120
Ms. Mi,

188
00:13:23,510 --> 00:13:25,360
it's not that serious. Calm down.

189
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:28,150
What era are we living in?
We can't go around fighting people.

190
00:13:28,150 --> 00:13:29,750
Violence is the last resort.

191
00:13:29,910 --> 00:13:31,360
We need to outsmart them.

192
00:13:31,390 --> 00:13:32,270
Right, right.

193
00:13:32,270 --> 00:13:33,720
T-That's right.

194
00:13:33,960 --> 00:13:35,760
H-How's your brain recovering?

195
00:13:36,240 --> 00:13:38,100
T-Try using it... think a little.

196
00:13:43,240 --> 00:13:44,440
If we want to guarantee a win,

197
00:13:44,440 --> 00:13:46,970
we'll have to try something
unconventional.

198
00:13:49,190 --> 00:13:55,040
[Bicycle Parking]

199
00:14:05,060 --> 00:14:12,170
[Accessible Route—Please Keep Clear]

200
00:14:25,550 --> 00:14:26,360
Ma'am,

201
00:14:27,270 --> 00:14:28,600
when did this happen?

202
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,470
He was doing fine
during surgery just now.

203
00:14:32,670 --> 00:14:35,000
I don't know what happened.

204
00:14:35,150 --> 00:14:36,790
My son...

205
00:14:36,790 --> 00:14:38,450
Please take care of yourself.

206
00:14:38,910 --> 00:14:40,770
I run a funeral service business.

207
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:42,480
Have you found anyone

208
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:43,670
to handle the funeral arrangements?

209
00:14:43,670 --> 00:14:44,630
No.

210
00:14:45,270 --> 00:14:47,030
No. It's just me now,

211
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:49,030
-and I don't know anyone who handles that.
-How about this?

212
00:14:49,030 --> 00:14:51,630
Would it be okay
if I took a look at the deceased?

213
00:15:06,750 --> 00:15:07,870
He's far too young.

214
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:11,150
Ma'am,

215
00:15:11,960 --> 00:15:13,720
we have the best morticians.

216
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:15,510
Don't worry about his missing hair.

217
00:15:15,510 --> 00:15:16,840
I promise we'll restore him

218
00:15:16,840 --> 00:15:19,270
to exactly how he looked
before he passed away.

219
00:15:19,270 --> 00:15:20,000
Ma'am,

220
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,360
fate brought us together.

221
00:15:22,870 --> 00:15:24,030
Would you give me the chance

222
00:15:24,030 --> 00:15:26,230
to see your son off on his final journey?

223
00:15:28,790 --> 00:15:29,670
It's settled.

224
00:15:30,790 --> 00:15:32,110
The hearse is downstairs.

225
00:15:32,110 --> 00:15:33,150
We're not taking him to the morgue.

226
00:15:33,150 --> 00:15:34,790
We're going straight to the funeral home.

227
00:15:34,790 --> 00:15:36,510
I'll take care of everything,

228
00:15:36,510 --> 00:15:37,200
from the funeral hall and flowers
to the ceremony and the banquet.

229
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,480
I'll make sure
it's all arranged perfectly.

230
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:40,010
How does that sound, ma'am?

231
00:15:41,720 --> 00:15:42,520
It's settled.

232
00:15:47,480 --> 00:15:47,910
Gang,

233
00:15:48,440 --> 00:15:49,200
forget about the operating room.

234
00:15:49,200 --> 00:15:50,080
Meet me on the first floor.

235
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:50,670
Now!

236
00:15:56,510 --> 00:15:57,320
Ma'am, ma'am,

237
00:15:57,440 --> 00:15:58,240
um...

238
00:15:58,320 --> 00:15:59,870
could I take a look

239
00:15:59,870 --> 00:16:01,330
at the death certificate?

240
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,200
I just had it here.

241
00:16:09,550 --> 00:16:10,480
Where did I put it?

242
00:16:10,480 --> 00:16:11,440
Look carefully.

243
00:16:11,960 --> 00:16:13,750
Without a death certificate
from the hospital,

244
00:16:13,750 --> 00:16:15,120
the funeral home
can't process the paperwork.

245
00:16:15,050 --> 00:16:21,050
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

246
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,230
Could you

247
00:16:16,230 --> 00:16:17,630
take my son there first?

248
00:16:17,630 --> 00:16:19,320
I'll bring the certificate over later.

249
00:16:19,320 --> 00:16:20,030
Well...

250
00:16:20,600 --> 00:16:21,150
Ma'am,

251
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:22,930
ma'am, my condolences.

252
00:16:23,750 --> 00:16:24,480
We offer

253
00:16:24,480 --> 00:16:25,910
full-service funeral services

254
00:16:25,910 --> 00:16:27,110
at the lowest prices,

255
00:16:27,200 --> 00:16:28,030
and we're

256
00:16:28,030 --> 00:16:30,200
the most professional
funeral home in the city.

257
00:16:30,200 --> 00:16:31,260
What are you doing?

258
00:16:32,080 --> 00:16:33,320
What are you doing here?

259
00:16:33,320 --> 00:16:34,670
Look, we're all civilized people here.

260
00:16:34,670 --> 00:16:35,870
Ma'am has already chosen my company.

261
00:16:35,870 --> 00:16:36,960
Why are you still trying
to steal her away?

262
00:16:36,960 --> 00:16:39,490
Weren't you supposed
to be waiting upstairs?

263
00:16:39,550 --> 00:16:40,200
Mr. Xu,

264
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:43,200
you can't just squeeze
every last penny out of people.

265
00:16:45,630 --> 00:16:46,150
Ma'am,

266
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:48,390
we've got connections
at the funeral home.

267
00:16:48,390 --> 00:16:49,870
We can sort out
the death certificate later.

268
00:16:49,870 --> 00:16:50,550
-I-I have connections there too.
-Hurry up.

269
00:16:50,550 --> 00:16:51,390
Take your son to the funeral hall.

270
00:16:51,390 --> 00:16:52,870
Isn't that monopolizing the business?

271
00:16:52,870 --> 00:16:54,360
I'm sorry, miss.

272
00:16:54,360 --> 00:16:56,480
-They got here first.
-I understand, I understand, ma'am.

273
00:16:56,480 --> 00:16:56,960
Ma'am.

274
00:17:12,550 --> 00:17:13,200
Wait,

275
00:17:13,720 --> 00:17:14,920
put him on top of the coffin.

276
00:17:14,920 --> 00:17:16,450
We usually put them inside.

277
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,109
On top, on top.

278
00:17:18,880 --> 00:17:19,880
All right, all right.

279
00:17:19,880 --> 00:17:21,750
Come on. One, two, lift!

280
00:17:25,880 --> 00:17:26,349
Ma'am,

281
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:29,040
would you like to sit in the front
or in the back?

282
00:17:29,200 --> 00:17:30,330
I'll sit in the back.

283
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,440
I want to spend a little more time

284
00:17:31,440 --> 00:17:32,150
with my son.

285
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:33,860
Be careful.

286
00:17:38,240 --> 00:17:39,400
Aren't you coming with me?

287
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,030
I've still got something
to take care of upstairs.

288
00:17:41,030 --> 00:17:42,480
But I can't do that.

289
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,640
You're the only person I know.

290
00:17:45,640 --> 00:17:46,440
If you don't get in,

291
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,720
who am I supposed to turn to later?

292
00:17:47,720 --> 00:17:48,270
Here,

293
00:17:48,590 --> 00:17:49,480
let me give you my business card.

294
00:17:49,480 --> 00:17:50,030
If you need anything,

295
00:17:50,030 --> 00:17:51,110
just give me a call, okay?

296
00:17:51,110 --> 00:17:51,720
No.

297
00:17:52,400 --> 00:17:53,680
If you're not getting in,

298
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:55,000
then take my son back down.

299
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,550
I'll go find that young woman
from earlier.

300
00:17:56,550 --> 00:17:57,000
Ma'am,

301
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,350
we're a legitimate business.

302
00:17:58,350 --> 00:17:59,350
Do you really think we'd cheat you?

303
00:17:59,350 --> 00:17:59,680
Look,

304
00:17:59,680 --> 00:18:00,960
here's our business license.

305
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:01,790
I don't want to see it.
I don't want to see it.

306
00:18:01,790 --> 00:18:02,310
I-I...

307
00:18:02,310 --> 00:18:03,110
Sir,

308
00:18:03,110 --> 00:18:05,160
please help me get my son down from there.

309
00:18:05,160 --> 00:18:06,030
Take us to the morgue.

310
00:18:06,030 --> 00:18:06,750
No, no.

311
00:18:06,790 --> 00:18:08,450
I'll come with you. All right?

312
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,530
Why are you so eager to help?

313
00:18:11,070 --> 00:18:12,000
How about this, ma'am?

314
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:12,830
I'll take you both there

315
00:18:12,830 --> 00:18:13,960
and make sure you're settled in
before I leave.

316
00:18:13,960 --> 00:18:14,480
Okay?

317
00:18:17,240 --> 00:18:18,370
That's more like it.

318
00:18:33,550 --> 00:18:34,920
Nice acting, San.

319
00:18:35,680 --> 00:18:37,280
What are you calling me, huh?

320
00:18:41,830 --> 00:18:42,550
I'd better

321
00:18:42,550 --> 00:18:43,640
get upstairs.

322
00:18:43,750 --> 00:18:44,440
The results should be out any minute.

323
00:18:44,440 --> 00:18:45,790
This is our chance to win the job.

324
00:18:45,790 --> 00:18:46,550
Okay.

325
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:48,480
Well, I'll head back first.

326
00:18:48,830 --> 00:18:50,240
If you and Cai Zhuzi

327
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:51,880
manage to land the job...

328
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,000
I'll let you know.

329
00:19:17,720 --> 00:19:19,510
Can you turn the AC up a bit?

330
00:19:19,680 --> 00:19:20,480
Gang,

331
00:19:20,830 --> 00:19:22,440
turn up the AC in the back.

332
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:23,040
You got it.

333
00:19:31,590 --> 00:19:32,510
What's that?

334
00:19:33,550 --> 00:19:34,590
What is that thing?

335
00:19:34,590 --> 00:19:35,350
What?

336
00:19:36,030 --> 00:19:37,960
Is that a big moth flapping around?

337
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:43,000
It's the middle of winter.
Where would you find a moth?

338
00:19:43,030 --> 00:19:43,590
There's nothing there.

339
00:19:43,590 --> 00:19:44,200
No,

340
00:19:48,270 --> 00:19:48,830
I...

341
00:19:48,830 --> 00:19:51,000
Maybe I've been so overwhelmed
with grief lately

342
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:52,400
that I'm hallucinating.

343
00:19:54,680 --> 00:19:56,350
I-I understand, ma'am.

344
00:19:56,510 --> 00:19:57,440
You still

345
00:19:59,000 --> 00:19:59,590
have a long life

346
00:19:59,590 --> 00:20:01,510
ahead of you.

347
00:20:02,640 --> 00:20:04,300
Please don't grieve too much.

348
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:10,440
I thought I heard something just now...

349
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:18,680
Did you hear that?

350
00:20:19,680 --> 00:20:20,590
Hear what?

351
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:21,640
What? No, you...

352
00:20:21,640 --> 00:20:22,640
-I didn't hear anything.
-S-Stop talking.

353
00:20:22,640 --> 00:20:23,550
-Sir.
-I heard it just now.

354
00:20:23,550 --> 00:20:25,270
-Don't scare me like that!
-Stop talking for now.

355
00:20:25,270 --> 00:20:28,670
-I'm not scaring you. Stop talking.
-I didn't here anything.

356
00:20:42,070 --> 00:20:43,160
It's moving!

357
00:20:44,350 --> 00:20:45,110
What

358
00:20:45,790 --> 00:20:46,880
the hell is that?

359
00:20:47,720 --> 00:20:49,070
Let me out!

360
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:56,270
[Fucheng Funeral Services]

361
00:20:54,680 --> 00:20:56,350
He's come back from the dead!

362
00:20:56,400 --> 00:20:57,920
Begin the intracranial procedure.

363
00:20:57,920 --> 00:21:02,250
Evacuate the hematoma and address
the cerebral contusions and lacerations.

364
00:21:02,400 --> 00:21:03,600
Is the position okay?

365
00:21:04,240 --> 00:21:04,880
Yes.

366
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:10,640
Bipolar forceps.

367
00:21:11,440 --> 00:21:12,110
Suction.

368
00:21:24,830 --> 00:21:26,240
Intracranial pressure is coming down.

369
00:21:26,240 --> 00:21:27,640
Brain pulsation is good,

370
00:21:28,030 --> 00:21:29,830
and there's no active bleeding.

371
00:21:29,920 --> 00:21:31,680
Her life should be out of danger now.

372
00:21:31,680 --> 00:21:33,200
It's too soon to relax.

373
00:21:33,680 --> 00:21:34,440
The CT scan shows

374
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,300
another hematoma deeper inside.

375
00:21:39,750 --> 00:21:41,480
Let's adjust the position.

376
00:22:03,400 --> 00:22:04,310
We've found it,

377
00:22:05,350 --> 00:22:07,350
but it's very close to the thalamus.

378
00:22:07,750 --> 00:22:09,000
It's too deep.

379
00:22:09,310 --> 00:22:10,880
It'll be difficult to operate there.

380
00:22:10,880 --> 00:22:11,790
If we leave it,

381
00:22:12,110 --> 00:22:13,680
the patient faces a high risk

382
00:22:13,680 --> 00:22:15,510
of hydrocephalus and cerebral edema,

383
00:22:15,510 --> 00:22:16,350
which could also

384
00:22:16,350 --> 00:22:17,550
affect her recovery.

385
00:22:18,240 --> 00:22:19,700
Are you going to remove it?

386
00:22:26,350 --> 00:22:27,310
Dr. Liu,

387
00:22:27,310 --> 00:22:29,310
the intraventricular hematoma is too deep.

388
00:22:29,310 --> 00:22:30,680
Should we remove it?

389
00:22:30,680 --> 00:22:31,310
Yes.

390
00:22:32,070 --> 00:22:33,510
If we leave it now,

391
00:22:33,680 --> 00:22:34,750
we're leaving the patient

392
00:22:34,750 --> 00:22:36,010
at risk after surgery.

393
00:22:38,240 --> 00:22:39,480
The patient is developing an arrhythmia.

394
00:22:39,480 --> 00:22:41,160
Blood pressure is dropping rapidly.

395
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:42,310
Sixty over forty.

396
00:22:45,350 --> 00:22:46,880
I understand

397
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:48,600
how much you want to make sure

398
00:22:48,720 --> 00:22:50,590
this surgery is done thoroughly.

399
00:22:51,640 --> 00:22:53,030
But no matter what,

400
00:22:53,880 --> 00:22:54,750
if the patient dies

401
00:22:54,750 --> 00:22:56,080
on the operating table,

402
00:22:56,680 --> 00:22:57,920
the family will see it

403
00:22:58,160 --> 00:22:59,550
as your fault.

404
00:22:59,830 --> 00:23:01,240
You're not as exceptional

405
00:23:01,240 --> 00:23:02,400
as you think you are.

406
00:23:08,110 --> 00:23:08,960
Dr. Liu,

407
00:23:09,270 --> 00:23:10,640
the collapsed brain tissue is swelling,

408
00:23:10,640 --> 00:23:12,310
and intracranial pressure is increasing.

409
00:23:12,310 --> 00:23:13,200
Blood pressure has climbed

410
00:23:13,200 --> 00:23:14,070
from 120 to 150.

411
00:23:25,200 --> 00:23:26,510
The hematoma is so deep.

412
00:23:26,510 --> 00:23:28,240
Are we still going to remove it?

413
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:29,240
Yes.

414
00:23:30,070 --> 00:23:33,070
We can't leave anything behind
that could pose a risk.

415
00:23:38,010 --> 00:23:43,000
[Starry Night] [Xiaoximen Hospital]

416
00:23:54,100 --> 00:23:55,850
[Authorized Personnel Only]
[Keep Quiet]

417
00:24:14,050 --> 00:24:16,660
[Please Press the Bell—Do Not Pull]

418
00:24:16,510 --> 00:24:17,440
The surgery was successful.

419
00:24:16,740 --> 00:24:19,260
[Operating Room]
[Authorized Personnel Only]

420
00:24:17,790 --> 00:24:19,990
The patient is out of immediate danger.

421
00:24:20,160 --> 00:24:21,400
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

422
00:24:21,400 --> 00:24:22,200
Get up.

423
00:24:22,350 --> 00:24:23,680
Come on, get up.
I can't hold you up much longer.

424
00:24:23,680 --> 00:24:24,350
I'll leave her in your hands.

425
00:24:24,350 --> 00:24:25,790
Thank you, Doctor. Thank you.

426
00:24:25,790 --> 00:24:26,440
Thank you.

427
00:24:28,510 --> 00:24:29,440
The hematoma evacuation

428
00:24:29,440 --> 00:24:30,720
went well.

429
00:24:30,830 --> 00:24:31,790
Intracranial pressure

430
00:24:31,790 --> 00:24:33,880
was significantly relieved
after hematoma evacuation.

431
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:35,480
Her condition is fairly stable for now.

432
00:24:35,480 --> 00:24:36,160
However...

433
00:24:50,920 --> 00:24:51,790
Dr. Liu,

434
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:53,260
how did the surgery go?

435
00:24:56,110 --> 00:24:57,510
What's going on with him?

436
00:25:25,640 --> 00:25:26,310
Thank you.

437
00:25:31,660 --> 00:25:34,080
[Department of Neurosurgery]

438
00:25:32,640 --> 00:25:33,440
Zhengliang.

439
00:25:34,150 --> 00:25:36,690
[Doctor's Office]

440
00:25:34,750 --> 00:25:36,810
you performed a remarkable surgery.

441
00:25:47,880 --> 00:25:49,790
Director, your phone's ringing.

442
00:25:50,780 --> 00:25:52,830
[Doctor's Office]

443
00:25:53,070 --> 00:25:54,930
Director, your phone's ringing.

444
00:26:18,960 --> 00:26:19,750
Hello?

445
00:26:20,070 --> 00:26:21,600
Hi, is this Liu Zhengliang?

446
00:26:23,160 --> 00:26:23,960
Speaking.

447
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:26,920
I'm calling
from East Suburb Police Station.

448
00:26:26,920 --> 00:26:27,680
Your younger brother

449
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:28,880
is here with us.

450
00:26:28,920 --> 00:26:30,050
Could you come down?

451
00:26:33,030 --> 00:26:34,440
Okay, I'll be right there.

452
00:26:34,440 --> 00:26:35,640
Please wait a moment.

453
00:27:14,480 --> 00:27:15,270
She's alive?

454
00:27:19,350 --> 00:27:20,240
Okay, okay.

455
00:27:20,400 --> 00:27:22,350
Next time, get your facts straight first,

456
00:27:22,350 --> 00:27:23,070
all right?

457
00:27:24,680 --> 00:27:26,030
You had me running around like crazy,

458
00:27:26,030 --> 00:27:26,880
making me dig all this stuff up,

459
00:27:26,880 --> 00:27:28,400
and now you...

460
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:30,750
Well, I didn't see that coming either.

461
00:27:30,750 --> 00:27:32,640
I'm honestly amazed.

462
00:27:32,830 --> 00:27:34,750
She was in such bad shape,
and they still managed to save her.

463
00:27:34,750 --> 00:27:35,880
That's incredible.

464
00:27:36,110 --> 00:27:37,880
Anyway, you don't have
to stay up all night anymore.

465
00:27:37,880 --> 00:27:39,010
Just get some sleep.

466
00:27:55,240 --> 00:27:56,160
Hi.

467
00:28:05,260 --> 00:28:07,940
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

468
00:28:08,710 --> 00:28:11,000
[Fucheng City Taxi]

469
00:28:11,270 --> 00:28:12,880
T-This is my taxi.

470
00:28:13,350 --> 00:28:15,110
Aren't you going to
the East Suburb Police Station?

471
00:28:15,110 --> 00:28:15,830
How'd you know?

472
00:28:15,830 --> 00:28:16,640
We're headed to the same place.

473
00:28:16,640 --> 00:28:17,240
Hop in.

474
00:28:22,790 --> 00:28:24,190
[Fucheng City Taxi]

475
00:28:24,260 --> 00:28:27,480
[Xiaoximen Hospital]

476
00:28:44,270 --> 00:28:46,130
Although no actual harm was done,

477
00:28:46,830 --> 00:28:48,690
deceiving people is still wrong.

478
00:28:49,200 --> 00:28:49,960
If Xiaoping hadn't

479
00:28:49,960 --> 00:28:51,000
kept putting in a good word for you,

480
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:53,060
I wouldn't have let you off so easily.

481
00:28:53,750 --> 00:28:55,950
Go home and reflect on what you've done.

482
00:28:56,110 --> 00:28:57,030
Yes, we will.

483
00:28:59,000 --> 00:28:59,790
Ms. Mi,

484
00:29:00,440 --> 00:29:01,880
you've got a good life,

485
00:29:02,440 --> 00:29:05,310
yet you keep getting involved
in these shady dealings.

486
00:29:05,310 --> 00:29:06,440
What am I supposed to say to you?

487
00:29:06,440 --> 00:29:07,240
Yes.

488
00:29:07,790 --> 00:29:09,790
Mr. Song, you're absolutely right.

489
00:29:10,110 --> 00:29:10,790
Mom.

490
00:29:11,160 --> 00:29:13,360
I'll make sure it doesn't happen again.

491
00:29:16,550 --> 00:29:17,410
Hey, young man.

492
00:29:18,070 --> 00:29:20,790
In this freezing weather,
you're wearing a T-shirt,

493
00:29:20,790 --> 00:29:22,000
thin pants,

494
00:29:22,550 --> 00:29:23,350
and slippers.

495
00:29:24,590 --> 00:29:26,880
I just came straight
from the operating room.

496
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:27,880
I didn't even have time

497
00:29:27,880 --> 00:29:28,750
to change.

498
00:29:29,070 --> 00:29:30,110
You're a doctor?

499
00:29:30,640 --> 00:29:31,200
Yes.

500
00:29:32,310 --> 00:29:32,790
Here,

501
00:29:34,960 --> 00:29:36,360
take these and keep warm.

502
00:29:36,720 --> 00:29:37,790
We've got more in the duty room.

503
00:29:37,790 --> 00:29:38,790
Are you sure it's okay?

504
00:29:38,790 --> 00:29:39,590
Take them.

505
00:29:40,920 --> 00:29:42,270
Thank you, Officer.

506
00:29:42,480 --> 00:29:43,310
I'll bring them

507
00:29:43,310 --> 00:29:44,550
back after my shift

508
00:29:44,550 --> 00:29:45,720
tomorrow morning.

509
00:29:45,750 --> 00:29:47,480
No need. I'll come pick them up.

510
00:29:48,200 --> 00:29:49,590
Which hospital do you work at?

511
00:29:49,590 --> 00:29:50,790
Xiaoximen Hospital.

512
00:29:54,480 --> 00:29:56,410
In that case, just bring them to me.

513
00:30:00,030 --> 00:30:00,640
Okay.

514
00:30:00,960 --> 00:30:02,290
I'll bring them. I will.

515
00:30:08,590 --> 00:30:09,520
Liu Zhengguang,

516
00:30:09,640 --> 00:30:10,790
look at you now.

517
00:30:11,400 --> 00:30:13,660
Since when did you
learn to lie and cheat?

518
00:30:15,750 --> 00:30:16,590
I'm talking to you!

519
00:30:16,590 --> 00:30:17,720
Cat got your tongue?

520
00:30:19,590 --> 00:30:20,400
Listen,

521
00:30:21,400 --> 00:30:22,550
wasn't I just

522
00:30:22,790 --> 00:30:24,510
in that body bag?

523
00:30:24,790 --> 00:30:25,720
I fell asleep

524
00:30:25,720 --> 00:30:27,450
for a few minutes, then woke up.

525
00:30:27,960 --> 00:30:29,310
It was pitch-black.

526
00:30:29,310 --> 00:30:30,400
And suddenly, it hit me.

527
00:30:30,400 --> 00:30:31,460
Mom is still alive.

528
00:30:33,270 --> 00:30:34,270
Don't think

529
00:30:34,270 --> 00:30:35,480
you can change the subject

530
00:30:35,480 --> 00:30:36,720
by spouting this nonsense.

531
00:30:36,720 --> 00:30:38,720
When we get back,
you're going to explain yourself.

532
00:30:38,720 --> 00:30:39,640
What nonsense?

533
00:30:39,640 --> 00:30:41,100
Who's spouting nonsense?

534
00:30:41,310 --> 00:30:42,750
A mother and her child
share a special bond, you know?

535
00:30:42,750 --> 00:30:44,550
T-The heart can sense it.

536
00:30:45,920 --> 00:30:47,270
Mom's definitely still alive.

537
00:30:47,270 --> 00:30:48,510
She's gone somewhere quiet

538
00:30:48,510 --> 00:30:49,830
to enjoy the time she has left.

539
00:30:49,830 --> 00:30:50,880
That's enough. Shut up.

540
00:30:50,770 --> 00:30:54,290
[Police]

541
00:30:54,350 --> 00:30:55,880
You need to recover from surgery.

542
00:30:55,880 --> 00:30:56,830
You're coming back
to the hospital with me.

543
00:30:56,830 --> 00:30:57,720
I'm serious! I...

544
00:30:57,720 --> 00:30:59,920
-I'm telling the truth.
-Get in the car.

545
00:31:01,060 --> 00:31:04,120
♪ A soul that came to earth
amid the cries ♪

546
00:31:01,240 --> 00:31:02,110
See you, Aunt Mi.

547
00:31:02,010 --> 00:31:05,530
[Police]

548
00:31:02,510 --> 00:31:04,310
-Hurry up and go back.
-Bye-bye.

549
00:31:04,600 --> 00:31:07,770
♪ Welcome to this city of haste ♪

550
00:31:06,350 --> 00:31:07,350
We're going home.

551
00:31:07,750 --> 00:31:09,270
Mom, you're not wearing enough today.

552
00:31:08,240 --> 00:31:10,430
♪ Grow taller, quick as you can ♪

553
00:31:09,270 --> 00:31:10,840
I should have brought you a jacket.

554
00:31:10,840 --> 00:31:13,190
♪ Learn how to find your footing ♪

555
00:31:11,070 --> 00:31:11,930
It's freezing.

556
00:31:15,430 --> 00:31:18,700
♪ A soul who hid
among the lanes and alleys ♪

557
00:31:17,590 --> 00:31:18,790
What are you doing?

558
00:31:18,790 --> 00:31:20,110
What's taking you so long?

559
00:31:19,180 --> 00:31:22,400
♪ A single turn, and the lamp
at the door grows distant ♪

560
00:31:20,110 --> 00:31:21,510
We're freezing our butts off here!

561
00:31:20,250 --> 00:31:24,330
[1314 Funeral Services]

562
00:31:22,830 --> 00:31:23,720
Exactly.

563
00:31:22,840 --> 00:31:25,150
♪ The ticket bears no way back ♪

564
00:31:25,110 --> 00:31:25,880
All right,

565
00:31:25,480 --> 00:31:27,860
♪ How like life it is ♪

566
00:31:26,070 --> 00:31:27,330
why is it so cold today?

567
00:31:28,030 --> 00:31:28,750
Get in.

568
00:31:28,750 --> 00:31:29,280
Alright.

569
00:31:29,960 --> 00:31:30,590
Let's go.

570
00:31:30,050 --> 00:31:33,350
♪ One who nestled close
on a winter's night ♪

571
00:31:30,590 --> 00:31:31,350
Let's go

572
00:31:33,710 --> 00:31:36,900
♪ A bite of food beside a pool of gaze ♪

573
00:31:37,460 --> 00:31:39,580
♪ When summer dusk arrives ♪

574
00:31:40,020 --> 00:31:42,130
♪ We'll go to see the flowers ♪

575
00:31:44,620 --> 00:31:47,870
♪ One who was stranded on the road ♪

576
00:31:48,280 --> 00:31:51,410
♪ Heels buried under unseen snow ♪

577
00:31:51,550 --> 00:31:52,350
I'll do it!

578
00:31:51,900 --> 00:31:54,140
♪ Don't panic—the journey is long ♪

579
00:31:54,510 --> 00:31:57,030
♪ Long enough to hold your pause ♪

580
00:31:56,830 --> 00:31:58,110
The surgery was successful.

581
00:31:58,110 --> 00:31:59,510
The patient is out of immediate danger.

582
00:31:59,190 --> 00:32:01,660
♪ May every road you take be safe ♪

583
00:32:00,350 --> 00:32:02,070
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

584
00:32:01,830 --> 00:32:05,920
♪ May the scenery stay simple
and carry you past regret ♪

585
00:32:06,440 --> 00:32:09,480
♪ Love deeply whatever comes to meet you ♪

586
00:32:10,010 --> 00:32:12,950
♪ And let those who leave be buried
under snow on the hills ♪

587
00:32:13,720 --> 00:32:16,140
♪ May you come home covered in dust ♪

588
00:32:15,310 --> 00:32:16,110
Sweetheart,

589
00:32:16,470 --> 00:32:20,350
♪ Held by what you love
as you roam the world and return ♪

590
00:32:16,880 --> 00:32:18,010
what's on your mind?

591
00:32:19,160 --> 00:32:20,270
I was thinking

592
00:32:21,240 --> 00:32:23,070
about that little girl we saved today.

593
00:32:21,500 --> 00:32:25,900
♪ Saying the flowers
by the door are truly beautiful ♪

594
00:32:24,590 --> 00:32:25,990
It's been weighing on me.

595
00:32:26,880 --> 00:32:28,160
When I saw her,

596
00:32:28,160 --> 00:32:29,750
there was a pool of blood on the ground.

597
00:32:29,750 --> 00:32:31,720
I scooped her up
and ran straight to the hospital.

598
00:32:31,720 --> 00:32:32,470
I mean,

599
00:32:33,240 --> 00:32:34,830
you'd think someone in my line of work

600
00:32:34,830 --> 00:32:36,030
would've seen it all.

601
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:39,310
But she's the first person

602
00:32:39,310 --> 00:32:40,590
who nearly died in my arms.

603
00:32:40,590 --> 00:32:42,350
You must've gotten it wrong.

604
00:32:43,750 --> 00:32:44,590
They said

605
00:32:45,160 --> 00:32:46,310
it wasn't that serious.

606
00:32:46,310 --> 00:32:47,240
Oh, come on!

607
00:32:47,240 --> 00:32:48,510
Am I talking nonsense?

608
00:32:48,510 --> 00:32:49,590
She was so close to me.

609
00:32:49,590 --> 00:32:51,160
I saw her eyes roll back.

610
00:32:51,160 --> 00:32:53,020
Look at all this dried blood on me!

611
00:32:53,830 --> 00:32:55,000
One of the doctors

612
00:32:55,000 --> 00:32:55,960
even said something

613
00:32:55,960 --> 00:32:57,590
about her brain being exposed.

614
00:32:57,590 --> 00:32:59,000
And they still saved her?

615
00:32:59,110 --> 00:33:00,170
He's just amazing.

616
00:33:01,270 --> 00:33:02,310
I mean

617
00:33:03,160 --> 00:33:04,720
Zhengguang's older brother.

618
00:33:04,720 --> 00:33:05,720
He's incredible.

619
00:33:06,070 --> 00:33:06,790
When he

620
00:33:07,400 --> 00:33:08,730
came out, he was so calm,

621
00:33:09,350 --> 00:33:10,640
never rushing.

622
00:33:10,640 --> 00:33:12,440
In this really deep voice,

623
00:33:12,720 --> 00:33:13,790
he told the family,

624
00:33:14,550 --> 00:33:16,410
"She's out of immediate danger."

625
00:33:16,790 --> 00:33:18,310
Then he turned and walked away.

626
00:33:18,310 --> 00:33:19,640
The way he walked off...

627
00:33:20,750 --> 00:33:22,510
so cool. Seriously.

628
00:33:22,590 --> 00:33:24,200
Now I get why his name

629
00:33:24,640 --> 00:33:25,500
is Zhengliang.

630
00:33:26,160 --> 00:33:28,020
Because "liang" means "bright,"

631
00:33:28,720 --> 00:33:29,960
like shining light.

632
00:33:29,960 --> 00:33:31,360
You know what I mean, Dad?

633
00:33:32,400 --> 00:33:33,550
You get it, Mom?

634
00:33:33,550 --> 00:33:34,480
Shining bright.

635
00:33:35,070 --> 00:33:36,640
Back when your dad

636
00:33:37,070 --> 00:33:38,880
would walk around the train station

637
00:33:38,880 --> 00:33:39,750
and come back with three wallets

638
00:33:39,750 --> 00:33:40,830
and six watches,

639
00:33:41,240 --> 00:33:42,350
I felt the same way.

640
00:33:43,110 --> 00:33:45,170
I'm not bragging about my glory days.

641
00:33:45,830 --> 00:33:46,960
Crime

642
00:33:47,350 --> 00:33:48,110
is wrong.

643
00:33:50,030 --> 00:33:51,350
Sweetheart, sweetheart,

644
00:33:51,350 --> 00:33:52,750
you've got a crush on him?

645
00:33:52,880 --> 00:33:54,000
So what are you gonna do?

646
00:33:54,000 --> 00:33:55,860
I'm gonna get him, no matter what.

647
00:33:59,510 --> 00:34:00,550
Honestly,

648
00:34:00,750 --> 00:34:03,280
the sight of him walking away
really got to me.

649
00:34:03,510 --> 00:34:04,240
I was gonna make my move

650
00:34:04,240 --> 00:34:05,440
right then and there,

651
00:34:05,790 --> 00:34:07,160
but then I thought, he's at work and all,

652
00:34:07,160 --> 00:34:08,440
so I'd better hold back a little.

653
00:34:08,440 --> 00:34:09,370
Here's the plan.

654
00:34:09,400 --> 00:34:10,360
Tomorrow,

655
00:34:10,480 --> 00:34:13,110
I'll start by taking over that shop

656
00:34:13,190 --> 00:34:14,280
across from Xiaoximen Hospital.

657
00:34:14,280 --> 00:34:15,110
Then I'll head over to Xiaoximen Hospital

658
00:34:15,110 --> 00:34:16,110
and make him mine.

659
00:34:16,710 --> 00:34:17,590
Just like me.

660
00:34:17,840 --> 00:34:18,670
You bet.

661
00:34:23,760 --> 00:34:26,110
Liu Zhengliang

662
00:34:27,070 --> 00:34:29,190
is Li Zhongling's eldest son, right?

663
00:34:30,000 --> 00:34:31,760
Doesn't he have a condition?

664
00:34:32,030 --> 00:34:33,030
So what if he does?

665
00:34:33,030 --> 00:34:34,320
He can get treatment.

666
00:34:34,510 --> 00:34:35,550
What if he can't be cured?

667
00:34:35,550 --> 00:34:36,550
Then so be it.

668
00:34:37,670 --> 00:34:39,840
Look, I've got kleptomania, too.

669
00:34:39,840 --> 00:34:41,190
Has that been cured?

670
00:34:41,670 --> 00:34:42,800
I get restless

671
00:34:43,960 --> 00:34:45,489
if I don't steal something.

672
00:34:46,230 --> 00:34:47,110
So what?

673
00:34:47,670 --> 00:34:50,440
Worst comes to worst,
every time I have an episode,

674
00:34:50,440 --> 00:34:53,040
I'll turn myself in
and face the consequences.

675
00:34:58,550 --> 00:34:59,410
Check this out.

676
00:35:01,800 --> 00:35:02,590
Amy!

677
00:35:04,230 --> 00:35:05,090
I just took this

678
00:35:05,320 --> 00:35:07,880
from Mr. Song's desk.

679
00:35:08,280 --> 00:35:10,480
Mr. Song didn't even notice.

680
00:35:10,920 --> 00:35:11,440
You—

681
00:35:23,550 --> 00:35:24,190
Sorry!

682
00:35:25,280 --> 00:35:26,940
Mr. Song, we were wrong again.

683
00:35:37,050 --> 00:35:43,510
[Emergency]

684
00:35:38,320 --> 00:35:39,070
Doctor,

685
00:35:39,710 --> 00:35:40,840
when will my daughter

686
00:35:40,840 --> 00:35:41,960
wake up?

687
00:35:43,030 --> 00:35:44,030
Didn't

688
00:35:44,670 --> 00:35:47,230
Dr. Liu explain this to you
before the surgery?

689
00:35:47,230 --> 00:35:49,290
There's no guarantee she'll wake up.

690
00:35:49,760 --> 00:35:51,820
You need to be prepared for that, too.

691
00:35:55,360 --> 00:35:55,880
Okay.

692
00:35:57,230 --> 00:35:58,000
Dr. Che,

693
00:35:58,320 --> 00:36:00,000
please give my daughter

694
00:36:00,230 --> 00:36:02,000
whatever good medications she needs.

695
00:36:02,000 --> 00:36:03,960
Money's no object.

696
00:36:10,190 --> 00:36:11,920
Let's see how things go first.

697
00:36:11,920 --> 00:36:13,000
If there's really no improvement...

698
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:14,110
Hi, I wanted to ask

699
00:36:14,230 --> 00:36:15,590
if Zhang Jiao was transferred

700
00:36:14,290 --> 00:36:22,500
[Emergency] [Red Zone]

701
00:36:15,590 --> 00:36:16,670
to the ICU after surgery.

702
00:36:16,670 --> 00:36:18,190
No, she's still in there.

703
00:36:19,000 --> 00:36:19,630
-Okay, thank you.
-No problem.

704
00:36:19,630 --> 00:36:20,560
You're welcome.

705
00:36:51,510 --> 00:36:52,150
President.

706
00:36:52,150 --> 00:36:53,480
Have a seat. Sit down.

707
00:36:53,800 --> 00:36:55,860
I just want to talk to you for a minute.

708
00:36:56,710 --> 00:36:59,240
You've worked
with Liu Zhengliang twice now.

709
00:36:59,710 --> 00:37:01,440
What do you think of his skills?

710
00:37:03,320 --> 00:37:04,840
In terms of surgical skills alone,

711
00:37:04,840 --> 00:37:05,760
I'd say

712
00:37:05,920 --> 00:37:07,070
even Director Nie at No. 1 Hospital

713
00:37:07,070 --> 00:37:08,070
can't match him.

714
00:37:15,190 --> 00:37:15,840
Doctor,

715
00:37:16,320 --> 00:37:16,920
thank you.

716
00:37:16,920 --> 00:37:17,840
Thank you, Doctor.

717
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:18,360
Thank you.

718
00:37:18,360 --> 00:37:19,290
You're welcome.

719
00:37:20,510 --> 00:37:21,590
In Shenzhen, someone like him

720
00:37:21,590 --> 00:37:23,480
would've been fired just like that.

721
00:37:23,480 --> 00:37:25,800
Just goes to show the gap
in medical standards.

722
00:37:25,800 --> 00:37:27,030
Since you're all here,

723
00:37:27,030 --> 00:37:27,550
I—

724
00:37:30,510 --> 00:37:32,240
I know what you're going to say.

725
00:37:33,030 --> 00:37:34,430
You want to leave, right?

726
00:37:35,360 --> 00:37:37,400
Saving that girl was your choice.

727
00:37:37,920 --> 00:37:40,850
Now that you've saved her,
you have to see it through.

728
00:37:41,320 --> 00:37:43,630
You've seen the conditions here
for yourself.

729
00:37:43,630 --> 00:37:44,800
If you leave

730
00:37:44,800 --> 00:37:46,800
and something unexpected happens,

731
00:37:47,440 --> 00:37:49,000
you'll never be able to forgive yourself.

732
00:37:49,000 --> 00:37:50,330
That's not why I'm here.

733
00:37:50,880 --> 00:37:52,400
I wanted to ask why Zhang Jiao

734
00:37:52,400 --> 00:37:53,920
wasn't sent to the ICU.

735
00:37:55,940 --> 00:38:00,130
[No smoking]

736
00:37:57,400 --> 00:38:00,400
That doesn't mean I've changed my mind
about leaving.

737
00:38:02,000 --> 00:38:03,590
The ICU

738
00:38:04,190 --> 00:38:05,190
is too expensive.

739
00:38:05,880 --> 00:38:06,840
What if we can't save the girl,

740
00:38:06,840 --> 00:38:08,710
but the cost ends up
crushing her parents first?

741
00:38:08,710 --> 00:38:09,800
But her dad said

742
00:38:09,800 --> 00:38:10,480
money was no object.

743
00:38:10,480 --> 00:38:11,800
And you believed him?

744
00:38:12,510 --> 00:38:13,280
Just look

745
00:38:13,280 --> 00:38:14,550
at their situation.

746
00:38:14,710 --> 00:38:16,190
Setting aside any judgments
based on their appearance,

747
00:38:16,190 --> 00:38:16,630
just look at

748
00:38:16,630 --> 00:38:17,670
how they had to scrape together

749
00:38:17,670 --> 00:38:19,030
2,000–3,000 yuan for medical bills.

750
00:38:19,030 --> 00:38:19,800
You can see
what kind of financial situation

751
00:38:19,800 --> 00:38:21,060
they're in, can't you?

752
00:38:21,070 --> 00:38:22,710
Then if they can't afford it,
why not just say so?

753
00:38:22,710 --> 00:38:24,970
What's the point of pretending they can?

754
00:38:25,630 --> 00:38:26,280
Dr. Liu,

755
00:38:26,550 --> 00:38:27,840
with all due respect,

756
00:38:27,840 --> 00:38:28,550
there are some things

757
00:38:28,550 --> 00:38:30,080
you just won't understand.

758
00:38:30,230 --> 00:38:32,280
People say that being poor
doesn't mean you lack ambition or dignity,

759
00:38:32,280 --> 00:38:33,630
but that's true of only a few.

760
00:38:33,630 --> 00:38:34,440
The poorer most people get,

761
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:36,070
the less pride they have,

762
00:38:36,110 --> 00:38:38,240
so all they can do is put on a brave face.

763
00:38:38,320 --> 00:38:39,920
He keeps saying,
"Money's no object," over and over.

764
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:41,360
He's not saying it to us.

765
00:38:41,360 --> 00:38:42,800
He's saying it to himself. Otherwise,

766
00:38:42,800 --> 00:38:44,230
-he wouldn't be able to keep going.
-Alright. Alright.

767
00:38:44,230 --> 00:38:45,590
You don't have to explain all that to me.

768
00:38:45,590 --> 00:38:46,850
Forget the ICU for now.

769
00:38:47,030 --> 00:38:47,880
Why didn't you do

770
00:38:47,880 --> 00:38:48,710
a ventricular puncture

771
00:38:48,710 --> 00:38:50,360
or monitor her intracranial pressure?

772
00:38:50,360 --> 00:38:51,880
The tubing
for intracranial pressure monitoring

773
00:38:51,880 --> 00:38:53,030
costs 3,000 - 4,000 yuan per tube.

774
00:38:53,030 --> 00:38:53,710
That's already a lot of money

775
00:38:53,710 --> 00:38:54,710
for them.

776
00:38:54,710 --> 00:38:55,400
Then how will you

777
00:38:55,400 --> 00:38:56,630
monitor her intracranial pressure

778
00:38:56,630 --> 00:38:58,150
and test her cerebrospinal fluid
going forward?

779
00:38:58,150 --> 00:38:59,230
We can do a lumbar puncture.

780
00:38:59,230 --> 00:39:00,760
It costs less than 100 yuan.

781
00:39:01,110 --> 00:39:03,110
S-So we're just making do with that?

782
00:39:03,110 --> 00:39:04,630
That's how small hospitals do it.

783
00:39:04,630 --> 00:39:06,290
It's a temporary workaround.

784
00:39:14,760 --> 00:39:15,550
A-All right.

785
00:39:15,550 --> 00:39:17,070
I'm going to lie down for a while, too.

786
00:39:17,070 --> 00:39:17,920
Call me right away

787
00:39:17,920 --> 00:39:19,120
if anything happens.

788
00:39:35,150 --> 00:39:36,280
Chen Junnan, you...

789
00:39:36,280 --> 00:39:37,480
how many times has this happened now?

790
00:39:37,480 --> 00:39:38,320
Every time you see a patient,

791
00:39:38,320 --> 00:39:39,320
I have to step in and bail you out.

792
00:39:39,320 --> 00:39:41,150
I'm about to lose
every last shred of dignity.

793
00:39:41,150 --> 00:39:41,920
Wait, I—

794
00:39:42,190 --> 00:39:43,230
Didn't I call you because

795
00:39:43,230 --> 00:39:45,110
I was trying to do right by my patient?

796
00:39:45,110 --> 00:39:45,590
Tell me,

797
00:39:45,590 --> 00:39:46,710
if I mess up the treatment,

798
00:39:46,710 --> 00:39:47,590
won't I embarrass you, too?

799
00:39:47,590 --> 00:39:49,280
Now you care about embarrassing me?

800
00:39:49,280 --> 00:39:50,510
Every time I go there,

801
00:39:50,710 --> 00:39:51,630
you should see the way

802
00:39:51,630 --> 00:39:52,710
those nurses look at me.

803
00:39:52,710 --> 00:39:53,770
Even the president

804
00:39:54,400 --> 00:39:55,530
calls you a screw-up

805
00:39:56,030 --> 00:39:57,230
and keeps using you as a topic
when talking to me.

806
00:39:57,230 --> 00:39:58,000
You didn't even know that, did you?

807
00:39:58,000 --> 00:39:59,000
Come on, I told you from the start

808
00:39:59,000 --> 00:40:00,280
I didn't want to get into No. 1 Hospital
through connections.

809
00:40:00,280 --> 00:40:01,550
You insisted on getting me in.

810
00:40:01,550 --> 00:40:02,110
And now you're saying

811
00:40:02,110 --> 00:40:03,400
I'm embarrassing you.

812
00:40:03,480 --> 00:40:05,190
What else could you have done
if I hadn't got you in?

813
00:40:05,190 --> 00:40:06,110
You should be thanking me!

814
00:40:06,110 --> 00:40:06,510
Without me,

815
00:40:06,510 --> 00:40:07,440
you'd be a good-for-nothing
for the rest of your life.

816
00:40:07,440 --> 00:40:08,230
You didn't even realize that, did you?

817
00:40:08,230 --> 00:40:09,320
T-Thank you.

818
00:40:09,320 --> 00:40:10,030
Fine, fine, thank you.

819
00:40:10,030 --> 00:40:10,630
Now get back inside

820
00:40:10,630 --> 00:40:11,480
and stop yapping.

821
00:40:11,480 --> 00:40:12,740
Look at that attitude!

822
00:40:12,760 --> 00:40:13,880
I'm your father!

823
00:40:13,880 --> 00:40:14,940
What are you doing?

824
00:40:15,670 --> 00:40:16,760
He's been quiet for ages,

825
00:40:16,760 --> 00:40:17,550
and you're still going on at him!

826
00:40:17,550 --> 00:40:18,110
I was just trying to scare him a little.

827
00:40:18,110 --> 00:40:18,840
You can't even do that!

828
00:40:18,840 --> 00:40:19,960
Look how old he is.

829
00:40:19,960 --> 00:40:21,280
And you're still threatening
to whip him with your belt.

830
00:40:21,280 --> 00:40:22,070
See that?

831
00:40:22,280 --> 00:40:23,710
I'm telling you, he treats me like this

832
00:40:23,710 --> 00:40:24,630
at the hospital, too.

833
00:40:24,630 --> 00:40:25,590
I have no face left

834
00:40:25,590 --> 00:40:27,000
in front of my colleagues.

835
00:40:27,000 --> 00:40:28,730
Now you care about saving face?

836
00:40:28,880 --> 00:40:29,920
Yes, I do! I want to save face.

837
00:40:29,920 --> 00:40:30,760
I'll quit

838
00:40:30,920 --> 00:40:32,110
and go work at Xiaoximen Hospital.

839
00:40:32,110 --> 00:40:33,000
You quit and see what happens.

840
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:33,630
Let's see if I'll still

841
00:40:33,630 --> 00:40:34,760
consider you my son.

842
00:40:34,960 --> 00:40:36,190
If you don't, who's gonna take care of you
when you're old?

843
00:40:36,190 --> 00:40:37,280
T-That's hilarious.

844
00:40:37,280 --> 00:40:39,740
Your mom and I
can have another kid in no time.

845
00:40:41,880 --> 00:40:42,670
You?

846
00:40:44,960 --> 00:40:45,820
Go ahead, then.

847
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:50,160
What does he mean by that?

848
00:40:52,510 --> 00:40:53,110
Hello,

849
00:40:53,190 --> 00:40:55,510
the subscriber you dialed is busy now.

850
00:40:55,630 --> 00:40:57,030
Please try again later.

851
00:40:57,070 --> 00:40:57,670
Sorry.

852
00:40:57,960 --> 00:41:00,670
The subscriber you dialed is busy now.

853
00:41:00,840 --> 00:41:02,190
Please try again later.

854
00:41:01,510 --> 00:41:02,210
Liu Zhengliang

855
00:41:02,340 --> 00:41:03,900
[Calls]

856
00:41:03,970 --> 00:41:04,820
Liu Zhengguang

857
00:41:06,510 --> 00:41:07,000
Hello?

858
00:41:08,000 --> 00:41:09,260
Where's your brother?

859
00:41:16,880 --> 00:41:17,630
Tell me,

860
00:41:17,840 --> 00:41:19,360
do you think our son was just talking

861
00:41:19,360 --> 00:41:19,920
out of anger, or did he mean it?

862
00:41:19,920 --> 00:41:20,960
He was definitely just angry.

863
00:41:20,960 --> 00:41:22,920
It's not like we're gonna
have another kid at our age.

864
00:41:22,920 --> 00:41:24,180
That's not what I mean.

865
00:41:24,400 --> 00:41:27,000
I'm talking about him wanting
to go to Xiaoximen Hospital.

866
00:41:27,000 --> 00:41:28,400
He was definitely just angry.

867
00:41:28,400 --> 00:41:30,930
What's so special
about Xiaoximen Hospital?

868
00:41:32,070 --> 00:41:33,280
Then why do I

869
00:41:33,360 --> 00:41:34,510
have a bad feeling about this?

870
00:41:34,510 --> 00:41:35,440
What do you mean?

871
00:41:35,960 --> 00:41:36,960
Think about it.

872
00:41:37,920 --> 00:41:38,960
Of all the places he could go,

873
00:41:38,960 --> 00:41:40,000
why does he have

874
00:41:40,320 --> 00:41:42,150
to go to Xiaoximen Hospital?

875
00:41:42,280 --> 00:41:43,140
Think about it.

876
00:41:43,710 --> 00:41:45,570
Who's at the Xiaoximen Hospital?

877
00:41:46,400 --> 00:41:47,440
Liu Zhengliang?

878
00:41:47,440 --> 00:41:48,320
Exactly.

879
00:41:48,760 --> 00:41:50,030
Didn't Liu Zhengliang just come back

880
00:41:50,030 --> 00:41:51,000
from Shenzhen?

881
00:41:51,280 --> 00:41:52,210
I'm telling you,

882
00:41:52,440 --> 00:41:54,590
that kid's been exceptional
since he was little,

883
00:41:54,590 --> 00:41:56,590
and he came back from a big city, too.

884
00:41:57,670 --> 00:41:59,000
Do you think our son

885
00:41:59,360 --> 00:42:00,510
wants to go

886
00:42:00,510 --> 00:42:02,640
to Xiaoximen Hospital because of him?

887
00:42:04,110 --> 00:42:04,910
You know what?

888
00:42:05,670 --> 00:42:06,320
I'm going

889
00:42:06,320 --> 00:42:09,190
to Xiaoximen Hospital tomorrow
to check things out.

890
00:42:09,190 --> 00:42:10,390
Let's get some sleep.

891
00:42:11,230 --> 00:42:12,320
Good grief.

892
00:42:59,190 --> 00:42:59,710
One.

893
00:43:00,480 --> 00:43:01,110
Two.
